{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "The Natural World", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Visiting the Sharks", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Identify and describe events in the news in a range of social and work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_9"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "massive ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very large ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Some sharks are massive!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about nature.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "great white shark", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a large species of shark", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It must be terrifying diving with a great white shark.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "too close for comfort", "type": "name"}, {"content": "dangerously or uncomfortably near", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Diving with sharks sounds too close for comfort.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to lure", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to tempt by offering some type of reward", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: People get in a cage and go down under the water as people on the surface lure the sharks to the area. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "element", "type": "name"}, {"content": "natural environment", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The sharks are in their element there - the humans are not! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to put yourself through ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to expose yourself to a difficult or dangerous situation ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You must love nature to put yourself through that. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "voluntarily", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to do something by choice ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I would never voluntarily dive with sharks!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob06aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " obsessed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having something occupy your mind most of the time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You must be really obsessed with nature.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob06aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "creepy ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "scary ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  It sounds really creepy, but interesting! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob06aud09", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Asking for Clarification and Emphasizing a Point", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You ask for clarification when you want more details of what the other person is talking about.<br/>You can emphasize a point by asking rhetorical questions. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">embedded questions </span> to ask for clarification. An <span class=\"strong\">embedded question</span> is a question inside another question or statement. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"strong\">Direct question:</span> <span class=\"italic\"> What was the show about sharks?</span><br/> <span class=\"strong\">Embedded question:</span> <span class=\"italic\"> Do you remember what that show was you watched about the sharks?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can also use <span class=\"strong\">rhetorical questions</span> to emphasize a point. Rhetorical questions are questions that don't have an answer. The speaker just wants to make a point about something. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Do you know how many people have been killed by sharks? </span> (The speaker doesn't really expect the listener to tell her how many people have been killed by sharks. Rather, she wants to emphasize the point that sharks are dangerous.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Do you remember what that show was you watched about the sharks?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Do you know how many people have been killed by sharks? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Do you mean to tell me that they go in the water? ", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Showing That You Understand Someone's Feelings", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">must</span> followed by an adjective when you want to empathize with someone. When you empathize with someone, you show them that you understand their feelings.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Here is the structure to follow:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + must + verb + adjective", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">You must feel depressed.<br/> You must be excited.<br/> They must be shocked! <br/> It must be terrifying to do that!</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use either <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span> adjectives or <span class=\"italic\">-ed</span> adjectives. <br>An adjective that ends in -ING is used to describe the characteristic of a person, a thing or a situation. <br> Example: <span class=\"italic\">This is a very interesting topic.</span> <br> <br> An adjective that ends in -ED is used to describe a feeling or an emotion. <br> Example: <span class=\"italic\"> I was bored at the concert.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compare the difference: ", "type": "text"}, {"content": " You must be obsessed with nature to put yourself through that.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Diving with sharks must be terrifying!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">He is bored. </span> (It means that the person is not having fun at the moment.) <br />  <span class=\"italic\">He is boring. </span> (It means that the person is tedious and makes other people feel bored.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Don't forget to include the verb before the adjective.", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Discuss the activity of diving with sharks with your partner. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talk about the advantages and disadvantages of doing an activity like diving with sharks.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Keep the conversation going by asking follow-up questions.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I discuss the topic of diving with sharks with my partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We keep the conversation going and show understanding of someone's feelings.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask for clarification and emphasize a point.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn7le12ob06re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn7le12ob06re2img05.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:         One thing I never want to do, and I see people doing on TV, is diving with sharks! That must be so terrifying! Especially the great white sharks! They're massive! <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:         I know! What do these people think they're doing?! I mean, I'm all about getting in touch with nature, but that's a little too close for comfort!<br/>"}, {"image": "engenn7le12ob06re2img01.jpg", "time": "20500", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:         No kidding! I saw this one show about shark diving in South Africa. People get in a cage and go down under the water as people on the surface lure the sharks to the area. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:         Do you mean to tell me that they go in the water? That must be so frightening! The sharks are in their element there - the humans are not! <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:         Do you know how many people have been killed by sharks? Why would you knowingly swim with them? Some people have too much time on their hands.<br/>"}, {"image": "engenn7le12ob06re2img02.jpg", "time": "50250", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:         Do you remember what that show was you watched about the sharks? I'm kind of interested in checking it out.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:         I think it was called <span class=\"italic\">Swimming with Sharks</span>. It'll give you nightmares! <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:         It sounds really creepy, but interesting! <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:         Wow, you must be really obsessed with nature to voluntarily put yourself through that. <br/>"}], "audiosrc": "engenn7le12ob06re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn7le12ob06re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [], "id": 2}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "  I can talk about nature and the animal world. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can show I u